 =?UTF-8?q?front-load=20MIDI=20parsing=20at=20init=20(eliminate=20mid-game?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20load=20spike)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0112, Phase 11 iter H opt #1). Pre-parse all 41
.mid files at engine init when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PRELOAD_MIDI=1
+ MIDI-routed backend selected. Eliminates the ~446ms mid-
gameplay file-parse spike per W22-WB-D PAUSE measurement
(operator-perceived "studder during disk write" on song change).

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PRELOAD_MIDI=1 strict-1, default OFF.

NEW MidiScheduler API (2 methods):
  add_to_preload_cache(path, cache_key) — parse file → store events
    vector under cache_key. Memory ~50 KB per track × 41 tracks ≈
    ~2 MB resident. Failed parses NOT cached (so subsequent
    load_from_preload_cache returns false → caller falls back).
  load_from_preload_cache(cache_key) — lookup map; if hit, copy
    events to _events + reset playback position; return true. If
    miss, return false (caller falls back to load(path)).

NEW MidiScheduler storage:
  std::unordered_map<std::string, std::vector<MidiEvent>>
      _preload_cache  (sized 0 when env unset; 41 entries when ON)

NEW SoundManager state + flow:
  bool _preload_midi_active member (default false; set at init from
    env var × backend-active check)
  init() block (after _reloadTrackList + after backend install):
    if env=1 AND backend ∈ {midi_stub, wb, opl3}:
      iterate _music_names[1..N] → add_to_preload_cache for each
      log preloaded/failed counts
    else if env=1 (no MIDI backend):
      log "skipped to save init time + memory"
  _start_mid_track(): if _preload_midi_active, try
    load_from_preload_cache first; fallback to load(path) on miss

DOS-PORT trade-offs (per dispatch):
  +400 ms one-time init delay (41 × ~10ms parse on PODP83-class)
  +2 MB resident memory (fits comfortably in 48 MB Tier-1 g2k)
  −446 ms mid-gameplay spike on song change (load_from_preload_cache
   is sub-ms vs file-parse 446ms)
  No effect when AUDIO_BACKEND=organya (preload skipped to save
   init delay + memory; Organya doesn't use .mid files)

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast, AUDIO_BACKEND=midi-stub + PRELOAD_MIDI=1):
  - 41/41 tracks preloaded at init: all named tracks parsed +
    cached in <1 sec emulated time. "preload complete — 41
    tracks cached, 0 failed" line confirms.
  - Runtime track change to curly: "load_from_preload_cache: hit
    'curly' = 5684 events" line fires — confirming cache lookup
    path engaged. Mid-gameplay file-parse path skipped.
  - 67 flips, no crashes.
  - strings-grep verifies SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PRELOAD_MIDI symbol +
    "preloading all tracks" + "preload complete" + "load_from_-
    preload_cache: hit" string templates all present.

DOSBox-X smoke validates structure; real-HW W22-WB-H iter PLAY1
will measure the actual fps gain from eliminating the mid-game
spike per dispatch's "real-HW iter validates fps gain" gate.

Per-track division note (preserved across cache hits):
  _division_ppq is set per-call from the SMF header. wiimidi
  set is 480 PPQ uniformly; orgmid set is 24 PPQ uniformly. First
  track preloaded establishes active division. If a future
  source dir mixes division values, cache hits would mistune
  playback timing for tracks with non-matching division. Robust
  fix would store division in the cache entry; deferred to
  wave-N+1 if real-HW iter shows tuning drift.

Out of scope (per silent_narrow_pattern.md):
  - LRU cache eviction (memory growth bounded at ~2 MB; no eviction
    needed)
  - Lazy preload (deferred to first-access) — defeats the purpose
    of eliminating mid-gameplay spike; init-time bulk preload is
    the essential approach
  - Cross-source-dir cache (key uses track name only; switching
    AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE mid-run not supported anyway since it's
    init-only)

Tier-1 64-bit-perf-validated path: real-HW iter packaging awaits
team-lead's iter H dispatch (3-PLAY: ORG / OPL3 / OPL3 with
preload).
